## Publication-Relevant Components Outside Direct Runtime Dependency Scope

These components are not counted in the direct dependency total above, but they affect release compliance and should be tracked for GitHub distribution.

| Component | Current Use | License / Notice | Source | Release Impact |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Open font pack | 22 bundled font files recorded in `fonts/open/open_fonts_manifest.json` | OFL-1.1 or compatible open font license | Google Fonts GitHub repository, TikTok Sans official GitHub release, and Adobe open-source font releases | Keep each font license file next to redistributed font files. Do not rename modified OFL fonts using reserved font names |
| FFmpeg BtbN GPL build | Code downloads `ffmpeg-master-latest-win64-gpl.zip` on demand | GPL variant of FFmpeg build; BtbN build scripts are MIT, packaged FFmpeg binaries include GPL/LGPL components | https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds | Do not silently bundle without preserving notices and source-offer requirements. Prefer documenting user-managed FFmpeg download or switching to an LGPL build if GPL distribution is not intended |
| PyInstaller | GitHub Actions build tool for Windows artifact | GPL-2.0-or-later with bootloader exception | https://pyinstaller.org/en/stable/license.html | Build outputs may be shipped under the project/dependency-compatible license; still keep build provenance |
| Playwright browsers | Browser runtime installed during release build | Chromium/browser component licenses | https://playwright.dev/python/ | If browsers are bundled into the PyInstaller output, keep browser notices under review |

## Compliance Baseline

Because the current direct GUI dependencies include `PyQt6` and `PyQt6-WebEngine` from PyPI under `GPL-3.0-only`, the open-source distribution baseline for this repository is `GPL-3.0-only`.

If the project owner has a Riverbank commercial PyQt/PyQt-WebEngine license, the project may choose a different project license, but that commercial entitlement is outside this automated audit and must be documented separately before release.
